Z||000013||frontal lobe||01-10-2001||06:54 PM||||I love the way the Raider fans get dressed up for the games.  Oh, what's that...they aren't "dressed up"?  Sorry.  My bad.<P>One of the worst things about the Oilers leaving is now I don't get to see their cool helmuts.  I used to love them.  I live too far north to care one way or another about the actual team or players.<P>Who should I root for that's left?<P>Ravens?  Kind of want to but hate Shannon Sharpe's big mouth too much.<P>Vi-queens?  Arch-rivals of my Packers but I don't care, Central division so I would root for them but wait, can't, HATE Cris Carter's big mouth too much and apparently so does Jim Haslett.<P>Giants?  Neutral on them but I wouldn't want New York area to have the World Series winner and Super Bowl winner.  Like NY doesn't already think the universe revolves around them.<P>Raiders?  L.A. or Oakland?  Oakland or L.A.?  Where can I make the most money?  Why do I wear sunglasses out of a bad Italian movie even on cloudy days?  John Gruden needs to have a b.m. BAD.  (I think.  That's the face my kids used to make when they did.)<P>I really can't decide.  Someone help me out here.  Persuade me.||||reg||1
Z||000014||kslish||01-10-2001||07:32 PM||||Well after the Steelers missed the playoffs with a 9-7 season I got behind New Orleans (Coach Haslett being an ex-Steeler coordinator and all, plus he played at and graduated from the college that I attended, Indiana University of PA).<P>After New Orleans went down, now it's Oakland who has won my respect with hard edged play and fans that may be almost as crazy as Steeler fans.<P>I don't like Baltimore because of owner Art Modell.  Period.  He took away one of the best rivalries in football (old Cleveland Browns versus the Steelers).  Those teams hated each other.  The fire just isn't there between the new Browns and the Steelers....at least not yet.<P>Ken S.<BR>'86 SC and '87 GT||||reg||5
